0217: precache every variant the current settings produce, keyed by canonical configs

A play session with enhanced lighting still compiled 137 pipelines on demand (100-180 ms frames).
They were variants of configs the shipped list held, or the same shader under another key:

- Canonical keys (gx::canonicalize_pipeline_config, applied in find_pipeline and to every known
  config): the destination alpha value is reduced to none / 0 / other (create_pipeline only tests
  those; the value is the draw's blend constant), and color channels / texgens the shader does not
  read are reset; depth-only copies drop the enhanced class (no enhanced shading; the class only
  appended uniforms). LM drew each ghost fade level with its own pipeline; the 5453-config list
  collapses to 1117 shaders.
- The rebuild expands every recorded config into the variants the current settings produce
  (queue_gx_variants): GX accuracy flags (as before), enhanced shader classes, the glow re-draw,
  the depth pre-pass and shadow-caster copies, the realistic flashlight's alpha-only cone
  (enhanced::precache_variants, from enhanced::precache_bits of the set configuration) and the
  early-Z alpha-test split pair (gx::early_z_split_variants), each for the targets it is drawn
  into. A change of those bits rebuilds the set like an accuracy flag change.
- A config met for the first time in play queues its own variants at once.
- aurora_pipeline_cache_get_stats: rebuildPending = pipelines queued by rebuilds not built yet (the
  application holds the game while they compile). MISS log lines name the config, the render
  target layout and the state.

